### Professional Summary

Senior ML Research Engineer with 10+ years of experience designing, implementing, and scaling deep learning systems across industrial, retail, and scientific domains. PhD candidate in Computer Science with strong foundations in linear algebra, calculus, and statistics. Proven track record of architecting novel model architectures, leading R&D initiatives, and mentoring ML teams. Experienced in translating complex domain problems into rigorous ML solutions and collaborating with cross-functional experts.

### Key Achievements

- **Architected a novel player experience embedding model** based on the Mamba (State Space Model) architecture to capture long-range behavioral patterns, reducing segmentation mismatches by 30% — demonstrating hands-on capability in designing cutting-edge deep learning architectures.
- **Reduced level design pipeline time by 40%** by engineering a Multi-Agent Generative AI framework (Claude, GPT) integrated with a custom simulation engine — showcasing expertise in generative models and agentic systems for complex design tasks.
- **Led the design and deployment of 15+ ML solutions** in production across forecasting, RAG/LLM, and adaptive control systems, generating >300% ROI for major enterprise clients and validating end-to-end ML system engineering skills.
- **Headed Data Science & Analytics at Rubbles**, managing a team of 20 DS/DA professionals across 5 parallel product integrations while building systematic review, assessment, and growth frameworks — demonstrating technical mentorship at scale.
- **Architected a "Digital Twin for Oil Manufacture" MVP**, simulating complex refining processes and interpreting ML models to identify dynamic properties of physical systems — directly transferable to molecular simulation and property prediction in scientific domains.
- **Designed and delivered a 30+ lecture Generative AI & ML course** at EPIC Institute of Technology, evidencing strong communication skills and ability to explain complex ML concepts to diverse audiences.

### Professional Experience

#### VOKI Games (Playrix)
*The #1 European mobile game publisher*

**Principal ML Engineer**
Sep 2025 – Present, Serbia, Novi Sad
- **Designed and implemented a novel deep learning architecture** based on Mamba (State Space Model) for player experience embeddings, capturing long-term behavioral dependencies in sequential data and reducing player segmentation mismatches by 30%.
- **Engineered a Multi-Agent Generative AI framework** (Claude, GPT) integrated with a custom gameplay simulator, automating Match-3 level creation and reducing design pipeline time by 40%.
- **Built a churn prediction classification model** to identify at-risk players, driving an estimated 20% LTV growth through targeted interventions.
- **Developed the enterprise-wide AI integration roadmap**, aligning ML research directions with product strategy.

#### Rubbles (SBDA Group)
*Company specializing in data-driven business process optimization for large enterprises.*

**Head of Data Science & Analytics**
Jan 2023 – Aug 2025, Serbia, Novi Sad
- **Led a team of 20 Data Scientists and Data Analysts** distributed across 5 parallel product activities, establishing systematic review, mentorship, and professional growth frameworks.
- **Owned and executed the Data Science roadmap** for the Retail business area, integrating ML-based demand forecasting and promo optimization solutions for major FMCG clients (KFC, Mars, Henkel, Unilever).
- **Built an internal LLM-based RAG system** (LangChain, FAISS, Hugging Face Transformers) for knowledge retrieval, reducing engineer onboarding time by 50%.
- **Served as primary technical liaison** to the CEO and C-level stakeholders, presenting ROI-driven performance reports and aligning AI strategy with business objectives.

**Lead ML Engineer**
Apr 2022 – Jan 2023, Turkey, Istanbul
- **Engineered demand and promo elasticity models** (LightGBM, XGBoost, Statsmodels) for Perfetti Van Melle, achieving a 15% reduction in stock-outs and 10% decrease in excess inventory.
- **Designed and deployed production-ready ML services** using PySpark and Docker, collaborating closely with backend engineering teams to analyze and review Java/Scala codebases, ensuring high-throughput data processing and seamless integration with backend infrastructure.
- **Mentored a cross-functional team of 5+ developers**, establishing best practices for code robustness, testing, and scalable AI infrastructure.

**Senior ML Engineer**
Nov 2021 – Apr 2022, Russian Federation, Moscow
- **Architected a global-scale demand forecasting system** for a leading QSR brand, improving WAPE by 12% through advanced feature engineering on large-scale tabular data.
- **Boosted campaign ROI and product availability** by implementing real-time traffic features, resulting in a 7% reduction in perishable food waste.

#### NDA (Confidential Client — Leading Oil & Gas Company)

**Senior ML Engineer / Head of Data Science**
Jun 2017 – Nov 2021, Russian Federation, Moscow / St. Petersburg
- **Led the Energy Efficiency & Cost Optimization R&D project**, developing dynamic regression models and factor analysis algorithms for energy consumption, achieving an estimated 5–7% reduction in energy costs.
- **Headed the Data Science department**, overseeing resource allocation across multiple IIoT projects and mentoring a cross-functional team of 6+ scientists and engineers.
- **Designed and deployed an automated anomaly detection solution** for oil production using deep learning (Keras, TensorFlow), reducing equipment downtime by 12%.
- **Architected a "Digital Twin for Oil Manufacture" MVP**, simulating complex refining processes and interpreting ML models to identify dynamic properties of technological objects — building scalable backend infrastructure (Python, K8s, Kafka) for scientific simulation workloads.
- **Led multiple R&D initiatives** including a platform for developing, serving, and monitoring multi-instrumental digital twin models, and an interpreted ML algorithm for dynamic property identification in complex physical systems.

### Skills and Technologies

- **Deep Learning & ML Research:** Deep learning architecture design, generative models, state-space models (Mamba), Transformers, anomaly detection, time-series modeling, simulation-based ML, digital twins
- **ML Frameworks:** PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras, Hugging Face Transformers, Scikit-Learn
- **Scientific Computing:** Python, NumPy, SciPy, Pandas, Statsmodels
- **Generative AI & LLMs:** Multi-Agent systems, RAG pipelines (LangChain, FAISS), prompt engineering, vLLM
- **Scalable ML Infrastructure:** PySpark, Docker, Kubernetes, Kafka, Azure, AWS, MLflow, Weights & Biases (W&B)
- **Engineering & Deployment:** FastAPI, Flask, ONNX, GitLab, Jenkins, CI/CD for ML
- **Mathematics & Statistics:** Linear algebra, calculus, statistical modeling, factor analysis, experimental design
- **Leadership & Communication:** Technical mentorship, cross-functional team leadership, stakeholder communication, scientific presentations, curriculum development

### Education

- **2021**: PhD Candidate in Computer Science — Peter the Great St. Petersburg Polytechnic University (SPbPU), Russia (ABD)
- **2017**: MSc in Technical Systems Management — SPbPU, Russia (Diploma with honors)
- **2015**: BSc in Computer Sciences — SPbPU, Russia
- **2013**: Erasmus Exchange — Czech Technical University in Prague (full program in English)

### Certifications

- **Agentic AI** — DeepLearning.AI (May 2026)
- **Generative AI with Large Language Models** — DeepLearning.AI / AWS (Jan 2024)
- **Advanced Data Science with IBM** — Coursera (Jul 2023)
- **Deep Learning Specialization** — Coursera (Jan 2021)
- **SQL for Data Science** — UC Davis (Sep 2021)

### Additional

- **Associate Professor** at SPbPU (Jan 2019 – Feb 2023): Developed and delivered AI courses to undergraduate and postgraduate audiences, demonstrating ability to communicate complex ML concepts across disciplines.
- **Lecturer** at EPIC Institute of Technology (Aug 2024 – Present): Created and taught a two-semester course on Data Science and Machine Learning (30+ lectures).
- **Expert** at karpov.courses (Mar 2024 – Aug 2025): Provided expert guidance on data-based decision making course materials.
- Fluent in English (C1, with teaching and presenting experience).
- **Prepared to relocate and self-fund relocation expenses**; visa sponsorship required.
</base_cv>

