y technical liaison to the CEO and C-level stakeholders.\n- **Owned and executed the Data Science roadmap** for the Retail business area, integrating ML-based demand forecasting and time-series models for major FMCG clients, increasing product availability by 5% on average.\n- **Built an internal LLM-based RAG system** (LangChain, FAISS, Hugging Face Transformers) for knowledge retrieval, reducing engineer onboarding time by 50%.\n- **Collaborated with backend engineering teams**, analyzing and reviewing Java and Scala codebases to ensure robust deployment of ML pipelines and seamless integration with backend infrastructure.\n\n**Lead ML Engineer**\nApr 2022 – Jan 2023, Turkey, Istanbul\n- **Engineered demand and promo elasticity models** (LightGBM, XGBoost, Statsmodels) on large-scale tabular data for Perfetti Van Melle, achieving 15% reduction in stock-outs and 10% decrease in excess inventory.\n- **Designed and deployed production-ready ML services** using PySpark, Spark, and Docker, ensuring high-throughput distributed data processing and seamless integration with backend infrastructure.\n- **Mentored a cross-functional team of 5+ developers**, establishing rigorous code review practices, unit testing standards, and best practices for scalable AI infrastructure.\n\n**Senior ML Engineer**\nNov 2021 – Apr 2022, Russian Federation, Moscow\n- **Architected a global-scale demand forecasting system** for a leading QSR brand, improving WAPE by 12% through advanced feature engineering on large-scale tabular datasets.\n- **Boosted campaign ROI and product availability** by implementing real-time traffic features, resulting in a 7% reduction in perishable food waste.\n\n#### NDA (Confidential Client — Leading Oil & Gas Company)\n\n**Senior ML Engineer / Head of Data Science**\nJun 2017 – Nov 2021, Russian Federation, Moscow / St. Petersburg\n- **Led the Energy Efficiency & Cost Optimization R&D project**, developing dynamic regression models and factor analysis algorithms