### Professional Summary

Senior ML Research Scientist with 10+ years of experience designing novel deep learning architectures and scaling ML systems for scientific and industrial applications. PhD candidate in Computer Science with rigorous foundations in linear algebra, calculus, and statistics. Proven expertise in architecting cutting-edge models (State Space Models, Transformers, Generative frameworks), leading R&D initiatives, and translating complex physical and chemical process challenges into robust ML solutions. Experienced in scaling training and inference for production-grade systems, collaborating with cross-functional domain experts, and mentoring research teams.

### Research Interests

Deep learning for scientific simulation, generative models for molecular and process design, state-space architectures, large-scale training and inference infrastructure, applied ML for real-world physical systems.

### Key Achievements

- **Architected a novel State Space Model (Mamba) for sequential player behavior embeddings**, applying advanced linear algebra and state-space dynamics to capture long-range dependencies, reducing segmentation mismatches by 30% — demonstrating world-class capability in designing new deep learning architectures from first principles.
- **Engineered a "Digital Twin for Oil Manufacture" MVP**, simulating complex chemical and physical refining processes and applying interpreted ML algorithms to identify dynamic properties of technological systems — directly transferable to scientific simulation and dynamic property identification for complex molecular and physical systems.
- **Reduced level design pipeline time by 40%** by engineering a Multi-Agent Generative AI framework (Claude, GPT) integrated with a custom simulation engine — showcasing hands-on expertise in generative models and agentic systems for complex design tasks.
- **Designed and deployed 15+ ML solutions** in production across forecasting, RAG/LLM, and adaptive control systems, generating >300% ROI for major enterprise clients and validating end-to-end scalable ML system engineering skills.
- **Mentored 20+ Data Scientists and Analysts** at Rubbles and 6+ cross-functional scientists at NDA, building systematic review, assessment, and growth frameworks — demonstrating large-scale technical mentorship and research leadership.
- **Designed and delivered 30+ lectures** on Generative AI and Machine Learning at EPIC Institute of Technology, evidencing strong ability to communicate complex ML concepts to diverse, cross-disciplinary audiences.

### Professional Experience

#### VOKI Games (Playrix)
*The #1 European mobile game publisher*

**Principal ML Engineer**
Sep 2025 – Present, Serbia, Novi Sad
- **Architected a novel deep learning architecture** based on Mamba (State Space Model) for player experience embeddings, applying state-space dynamics and linear algebra to capture long-term behavioral dependencies in sequential data, reducing player segmentation mismatches by 30%.
- **Engineered a Multi-Agent Generative AI framework** (Claude, GPT) integrated with a custom gameplay simulator, automating Match-3 level creation and reducing design pipeline time by 40%.
- **Built and deployed a churn classification model** (XGBoost) on large-scale tabular behavioral data to identify at-risk players, driving an estimated 20% LTV growth through targeted interventions.
- **Developed the enterprise-wide AI integration roadmap**, aligning ML research directions with product strategy and cross-functional stakeholder objectives.

#### Rubbles (SBDA Group)
*Company specializing in data-driven business process optimization for large enterprises.*

**Head of Data Science & Analytics**
Jan 2023 – Aug 2025, Serbia, Novi Sad
- **Led a team of 20 Data Scientists and Data Analysts** across 5 parallel product activities, establishing systematic review, mentorship, and professional growth frameworks; served as primary technical liaison to the CEO and C-level stakeholders.
- **Owned and executed the Data Science roadmap** for the Retail business area, integrating ML-based demand forecasting and time-series models for major FMCG clients, increasing product availability by 5% on average.
- **Built an internal LLM-based RAG system** (LangChain, FAISS, Hugging Face Transformers) for knowledge retrieval, reducing engineer onboarding time by 50%.
- **Collaborated with backend engineering teams**, analyzing and reviewing Java and Scala codebases to ensure robust deployment of ML pipelines and seamless integration with backend infrastructure.

**Lead ML Engineer**
Apr 2022 – Jan 2023, Turkey, Istanbul
- **Engineered demand and promo elasticity models** (LightGBM, XGBoost, Statsmodels) on large-scale tabular data for Perfetti Van Melle, achieving 15% reduction in stock-outs and 10% decrease in excess inventory.
- **Designed and deployed production-ready ML services** using PySpark, Spark, and Docker, ensuring high-throughput distributed data processing and seamless integration with backend infrastructure.
- **Mentored a cross-functional team of 5+ developers**, establishing rigorous code review practices, unit testing standards, and best practices for scalable AI infrastructure.

**Senior ML Engineer**
Nov 2021 – Apr 2022, Russian Federation, Moscow
- **Architected a global-scale demand forecasting system** for a leading QSR brand, improving WAPE by 12% through advanced feature engineering on large-scale tabular datasets.
- **Boosted campaign ROI and product availability** by implementing real-time traffic features, resulting in a 7% reduction in perishable food waste.

#### NDA (Confidential Client — Leading Oil & Gas Company)

**Senior ML Engineer / Head of Data Science**
Jun 2017 – Nov 2021, Russian Federation, Moscow / St. Petersburg
- **Led the Energy Efficiency & Cost Optimization R&D project**, developing dynamic regression models and factor analysis algorithms for energy consumption, achieving an estimated 5–7% reduction in energy costs.
- **Headed the Data Science department**, overseeing resource allocation across multiple IIoT projects, mentoring a cross-functional team of 6+ scientists and engineers, and championing ML adoption company-wide.
- **Designed and deployed an automated anomaly detection solution** for oil production using deep learning (Keras, TensorFlow), reducing equipment downtime by 12%.
- **Architected a "Digital Twin for Oil Manufacture" MVP**, simulating complex chemical and physical refining processes, building scalable backend infrastructure (Python, K8s, Kafka), and applying interpreted ML algorithms to identify dynamic properties of technological objects — directly transferable to scientific simulation and dynamic property identification for complex molecular and physical systems.
- **Led multiple R&D initiatives**, including a platform for developing, serving, and monitoring multi-instrumental digital twin models, and an interpreted ML algorithm for dynamic property identification in complex physical systems.
- **Collaborated closely with domain experts** (process engineers, metallurgists, control systems specialists) to translate complex physical and chemical process requirements into rigorous ML formulations.

### Skills and Technologies

- **Deep Learning & ML Research:** Novel architecture design (State Space Models/Mamba, Transformers), generative models, multi-agent systems, anomaly detection, time-series modeling, simulation-based ML, digital twins, scientific simulation
- **ML Frameworks:** PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras, Hugging Face Transformers, Scikit-Learn
- **Scientific Computing:** Python, NumPy, SciPy, Pandas, Statsmodels — strong foundations in linear algebra, calculus, and statistics for ML model development
- **Generative AI & LLMs:** Multi-Agent systems, RAG pipelines (LangChain, FAISS, Qdrant), prompt engineering, vLLM
- **Scalable ML Infrastructure:** PySpark, Spark, Docker, Kubernetes, Kafka, Azure, AWS, MLflow, Weights & Biases (W&B), CI/CD for ML
