ated 5–7% reduction in energy costs. Analyzed and tuned experimental results to inform future experimental directions and optimize energy resource allocation.\n- **Headed the Data Science department**, overseeing resource allocation across multiple IIoT projects, mentoring a cross-functional team of 6+ scientists and engineers, and championing ML adoption company-wide. Cultivated an inclusive R&D environment, encouraging diverse perspectives and fostering collaborative research culture.\n- **Designed and deployed an automated anomaly detection solution** for oil production using deep learning (Keras, TensorFlow), reducing equipment downtime by 12%.\n- **Architected a \"Digital Twin for Oil Manufacture\" MVP**, simulating complex chemical and physical refining processes using SciPy and NumPy for scientific computing, building scalable backend infrastructure (Python, K8s, Kafka), and applying interpreted ML algorithms to identify dynamic properties of technological objects — directly transferable to chemical data handling, molecular simulation, and dynamic property identification for complex molecular and physical systems.\n- **Led multiple R&D initiatives**, including a platform for developing, serving, and monitoring multi-instrumental digital twin models, and an interpreted ML algorithm for dynamic property identification in complex physical systems.\n- **Collaborated iteratively with domain experts** (process engineers, metallurgists, control systems specialists) to translate complex chemical and physical process requirements into rigorous ML formulations, sharing domain experience and iterating on experimental designs.\n\n### Skills and Technologies\n\n- **Deep Learning & ML Research:** Novel architecture design (State Space Models/Mamba, Transformers), generative models, multi-agent systems, anomaly detection, time-series modeling, simulation-based ML, digital twins, scientific simulation, chemical process modeling\n- **ML Frameworks:** PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras, Hugging Face Transformers, Scikit-Learn\n- **Scientific Computing:** Python, NumPy, SciPy, Pandas, Statsmodels — strong foundations in linear algebra, calculus, and statistics for ML model development\n- **Generative AI & LLMs:** Multi-Agent systems, RAG pipelines (LangChain, FAISS, Qdrant), prompt engineering, vLLM\n- **Scalable ML Infrastructure:** PySpark, Spark, Docker, Kubernetes, Kafka, Azure, AWS, MLflow, Weights & Biases (W&B), CI/CD for ML — extensive experience scaling training and inference engineering frameworks\n- **Engineering & Deployment:** FastAPI, Flask, ONNX, GitLab, Jenkins\n- **3D & Computer Vision (Foundational):** OpenCV, OpenGL, 3D modeling systems for strength characteristics analysis\n- **Mathematics & Statistics:** Linear algebra, calculus, statistical modeling, factor analysis, experimental design\n- **Leadership & Communication:** Technical mentorship, cross-functional team leadership, stakeholder communication, scientific presentations, curriculum development, fostering diverse and inclusive research culture\n\n### Education\n\n- **2021**: PhD Candidate in Computer Science — Peter the Great St. Petersburg Polytechnic University (SPbPU), Russia (ABD — All But Dissertation)\n- **2017**: MSc in Technical Systems Management — SPbPU, Russia (Diploma with honors)\n- **2015**: BSc in Computer Sciences — SPbPU, Russia\n- **2013**: Erasmus Exchange — Czech Technical University in Prague (full program in English)\n\n### Certifications\n\n- **Agentic AI** — DeepLearning.AI (May 2026)\n- **Generative AI with Large Language Models** — DeepLearning.AI / AWS (Jan 2024)\n- **Advanced Data Science with IBM** — Coursera (Jul 2023)\n- **Deep Learning Specialization** — Coursera (Jan 2021)\n- **SQL for Data Science** — UC Davis (Sep 2021)\n\n### Additional\n\n- **Associate Professor** at SPbPU (Jan 2019 – Feb 2023): Developed and delivered AI courses to undergraduate and postgraduate audiences, evidencing strong cross-disciplinary communication and teaching capabilities.\n- **Lecturer** at EPIC Institute of Technology (Aug 2024 – Present): Designed and taught a two-semester course on Data Science and Machine Learning (30+ lectures).\n- **Expert** at karpov.courses (Mar 2024 – Aug 2025): Provided expert guidance on data-based decision making course materials.\n- Fluent in English (C1, with extensive teaching and presenting experience).\n- **Prepared to relocate to London, UK and self-fund relocation expenses**; visa sponsorship required."
