### Professional Summary

Senior ML Engineer with deep **PyTorch** and **Python** expertise and hands-on experience designing and executing training loops for transformer-based architectures, including state-space models (Mamba/SSM). Strong engineering foundation in distributed data systems (PySpark, Kafka), production ML infrastructure (Docker, Kubernetes), and large-scale pipeline design. Track record of building high-performance ML systems, systematically optimizing model behavior and data pipelines, and delivering measurable business impact at enterprise scale. Collaborative engineer experienced partnering with researchers and stakeholders to align technical decisions with product goals.

*Note: Based in Serbia and prepared to relocate to Germany (Heidelberg) at my own expense; visa sponsorship support required only for the work permit process.*

### Key Achievements

- Designed and trained a player experience embedding model using the **Mamba (SSM)** architecture in **PyTorch**, capturing long-term behavioral patterns and reducing player segmentation mismatches by **30%**.
- Architected and scaled ML demand forecasting pipelines (**Python, PySpark, LightGBM, Docker, K8s**) across major FMCG clients (KFC, Mars, Henkel, Unilever), increasing product availability by **5%** on average.
- Built and deployed **15+ ML solutions** in production across forecasting, RAG/LLM, and adaptive UX — generating **>300% ROI** and reducing operational costs for major enterprise clients.
- Reduced Match-3 level development time by **40%** via a Multi-Agent GenAI pipeline (Claude, GPT) integrated with a custom gameplay simulator.
- Engineered a Digital Twin MVP for oil refining (**Python, TensorFlow, Kafka, K8s**), simulating complex industrial processes and accelerating R&D cycles for complex industrial assets.
- Drove **~20% LTV** growth and reduced churn by **50%** through ML-based adaptive user experience control systems.
- Designed and taught Generative AI & ML course (**30+ lectures**) at EPIC Institute of Technology.

### Tech Stack

- **Languages:** Python, C++, SQL
- **Deep Learning:** PyTorch, TensorFlow, Keras, Hugging Face Transformers, Mamba (SSM), ONNX
- **LLM & GenAI:** vLLM, LangChain, FAISS, RAG pipelines, Multi-Agent systems, Claude, GPT
- **Distributed & Data Systems:** PySpark, Databricks, Kafka, Docker, Kubernetes, Airflow
- **ML Libraries:** Pandas, NumPy, SciPy, Scikit-Learn, LightGBM, XGBoost, CatBoost, Statsmodels
- **Engineering & Tooling:** GitLab, Jenkins, Weights & Biases (W&B), MLflow, FastAPI, Flask, Dash

### Professional Experience

#### VOKI Games (Playrix)
*The #1 European mobile game publisher*

**Principal ML Engineer**
Sep 2025 – Present, Serbia, Novi Sad
- Designed and executed a custom **PyTorch** training loop for a player experience embedding model based on the **Mamba (SSM)** architecture, capturing long-term behavioral sequences and reducing player segmentation mismatches by **30%**.
- Built a churn prediction system in PyTorch to identify at-risk players, driving an estimated **20% LTV** growth.
- Developed a Multi-Agent GenAI framework (Claude, GPT) integrated with a custom gameplay simulator, automating Match-3 level creation and reducing the level design pipeline time by **40%**.
- Owned the roadmap for enterprise-wide AI integration, aligning model development with product strategy and engineering priorities.

#### Rubbles (SBDA Group)
*Data-driven business process optimization for large enterprises.*

**Head of Data Science & Analytics**
Jan 2023 – Aug 2025, Serbia, Novi Sad
- Led end-to-end design, scaling, and integration of ML demand forecasting pipelines (**Python, PySpark, LightGBM, Docker, K8s**) for KFC, Mars, Henkel, and Unilever, increasing product availability by **5%** on average across deployments.
- Built an internal LLM-based RAG system (**Python, LangChain, FAISS, Hugging Face Transformers**) for knowledge retrieval across engineering documentation, reducing onboarding time by **50%** for new engineers.
- Managed cross-functional delivery across **5 parallel integrations**, mentored a team of 5+ developers, and established engineering best practices for code robustness, testing, and scalable AI infrastructure.
- Served as primary technical liaison for the CEO and C-level stakeholders, aligning AI roadmaps with business goals and presenting ROI-driven performance reports.

**Lead ML Engineer**
Apr 2022 – Jan 2023, Turkey, Istanbul
- Engineered demand and promo elasticity models (**Python, LightGBM, XGBoost, Statsmodels**) for Perfetti Van Melle, reducing stock-outs by **15%** and excess inventory by **10%**.
- Designed and deployed production-ready ML services using **PySpark** and **Docker**, ensuring high-throughput distributed data processing and seamless integration with backend infrastructure.
- Led a cross-functional team of 3+ engineers, establishing rigorous code review and unit testing standards for production ML systems.

**Senior ML Engineer**
Nov 2021 – Apr 2022, Russian Federation, Moscow
- Architected a global-scale demand forecasting system for a leading QSR brand, improving WAPE by **12%** through advanced feature engineering and pipeline optimization.
- Boosted campaign ROI and product availability by implementing real-time traffic features in the data pipeline, reducing perishable food waste by **7%**.

#### NDA (Confidential Client)
*Largest gas producer and top oil and gas company.*

**Senior ML Engineer**
Jun 2017 – Nov 2021, Russian Federation, Moscow
- Architected a "Digital Twin for Oil Manufacture" MVP using **Python, TensorFlow, and Keras**, simulating complex refining processes. Built the scalable backend (**Python, K8s, Kafka**) and interpreted ML models to identify dynamic properties of technological objects, accelerating R&D cycles.
- Led the Energy Efficiency & Cost Optimization project, developing dynamic ML models and factor analysis algorithms for energy consumption, achieving an estimated **5–7% reduction** in energy costs.
- Headed the Data Science department, overseeing resource allocation across multiple IIoT projects and mentoring a cross-functional team of **6+** engineers.
- Designed and deployed an automated anomaly detection solution for oil production (**Keras, TensorFlow**), reducing equipment downtime by **12%**.
- Collaborated tightly with backend engineering teams by analyzing and reviewing existing Java and Scala codebases to ensure robust deployment of ML pipelines.

### Education

