  "cv_text": "## Senior ML Engineer | Training Efficiency & Distributed Systems\n\nExpert in profiling and optimizing large-scale model training throughput on GPU clusters, with deep experience in composite parallelism tuning, GPU kernel optimization, and hardware-aware architecture design. Skilled in PyTorch, NCCL, MPI, PyTorch Profiler, and Nsight Systems, with a proven track record of eliminating Python‑layer and GPU kernel bottlenecks to maximize hardware utilization.\n\n### Key Achievements\n\n- Enhanced model throughput by **40 %** for large‑scale GPU workloads through rigorous profiling with PyTorch Profiler and Nsight Systems, identifying and resolving Python‑layer and kernel‑level bottlenecks.\n- Tuned parallelization strategies (data parallelism, FSDP) for distributed LLM training, optimizing sharding, communication‑computation overlap, and minimizing critical‑path overhead on multi‑GPU clusters.\n- Championed mixed‑precision training (FP16/FP8) across ML pipelines, accelerating training speed while preserving model convergence and reducing GPU memory pressure.\n- Partnered with AI researchers to co‑design efficient model architectures, ensuring alignment between hardware utilization and training convergence objectives.\n\n### Skills\n\n- **Core Languages & Frameworks:** Python, PyTorch, CUDA, SQL\n- **Distributed & HPC:** NCCL, MPI, PyTorch Distributed (DDP, FSDP), Mixed‑Precision Training (FP16/BF16/FP8)\n- **Profiling & Optimization:** PyTorch Profiler, Nvidia Nsight Systems, Composite Parallelism (TP/DP/FSDP), GPU kernel analysis\n- **LLM & Serving:** Transformers, vLLM, Hugging Face, RAG pipelines\n- **Infrastructure:** Docker, Kubernetes, Databricks, PySpark, Azure\n\n### Professional Experience\n\n**VOKI Games (Playrix)** – Senior/Principal ML Engineer (Sep 2025 – Present)\n- Profiled and optimized model training and inference across GPU clusters using PyTorch Profiler and Nsight Systems, achieving **40 %** throughput improvement by eliminating Python‑level and GPU‑kernel bottlenecks.\n- Collaborated with AI researchers to define model architectures that maximized GPU occupancy while preserving convergence, directly informing hardware‑efficient design choices.\n- Implemented mixed‑precision training workflows, reducing memory footprint and accelerating training cycles for transformer‑based models.\n- Developed a Mamba‑based embedding model, applying efficient transformer training techniques and data pipelines to improve long‑sequence modeling.\n\n**Rubbles (SBDA Group)** – Head of Data Science & Analytics (Jan 2023 – Aug 2025)\n- Built an LLM‑based RAG system, optimizing Tensor‑Parallel and FP16 inference on GPU instances, reducing query response time by **50 %**.\n- Configured distributed data processing pipelines with Databricks and PySpark to feed large‑scale training workloads, ensuring high throughput and minimal I/O stalls.\n- Mentored engineers on scalable ML infrastructure and profiling‑driven performance optimization.\n\n**Rubbles (SBDA Group)** – Lead ML Engineer (Apr 2022 – Jan 2023)\n- Engineered demand forecasting models with LightGBM and XGBoost, streamlining batch inference on containerized GPU services to handle high‑throughput retail data streams.\n\n**NDA (Confidential)** – Senior ML Engineer (Jun 2017 – Nov 2021)\n- Orchestrated distributed model training using TensorFlow and PyTorch across on‑premise GPU clusters, leveraging NCCL for inter‑GPU communication and mixed‑precision to accelerate convergence.\n- Deployed a high‑availability real‑time anomaly detection system, tuning GPU inference to minimize latency for industrial IIoT applications.\n- Led the Data Science department, embedding performance‑first engineering practices and reviewing code for memory‑ and compute‑efficient model implementations.\n\n### Education\n- PhD Candidate in Computer Science (ABD) – SPbPU, 2021\n- MSc in Technical Systems Management (Honors) – SPbPU, 2017\n- BSc in Computer Sciences – SPbPU, 2015\n- Erasmus Exchange – Czech Technical University in Prague, 2013\n\n### Languages\n- English: Proficient (C1) – Teaching and Presenting Experience\n- Russian: Native\n\n### Additional Information\nReady to relocate; prepared to self‑fund all relocation and accommodation expenses. Requires only standard visa sponsorship."
