## Key Achievements

- Engineered and scaled high-throughput ML pipelines with PySpark and Databricks for global demand forecasting, increasing product availability by 5% and processing terabytes of retail data with sub-hour latency.
- Architected an efficient state-space model (Mamba) for long-term behavioral pattern recognition, reducing segmentation error by 30% while maintaining computational efficiency on GPU infrastructure.
- Built and optimized an LLM-based retrieval-augmented generation system on Kubernetes, cutting engineer onboarding time by 50% and demonstrating hands‑on expertise in transformer architectures and inference tuning.

## Professional Experience

### VOKI Games (Playrix) — Principal ML Engineer
*Sep 2025 – Present | Novi Sad, Serbia*

- Developed a churn prediction model on user telemetry data, driving a 20% lift in lifetime value through advanced feature engineering and training pipeline optimization.
- Designed and implemented a player experience embedding model using the Mamba (SSM) architecture to capture long-term behavioral signals; reduced segmentation mismatches by 30% while maintaining model throughput on production GPUs.
- Led cross‑functional collaboration with game designers and backend engineers to integrate ML features, ensuring robustness and low‑latency serving of models in a high‑QPS environment.

### Rubbles (SBDA Group) — Head of Data Science & Analytics
*Jan 2023 – Aug 2025 | Novi Sad, Serbia*

- Spearheaded the development of ML demand forecasting toolkits (PySpark, Databricks) for FMCG clients, optimizing ETL pipelines and model inference to achieve a 5% average improvement in product availability while meeting strict throughput SLAs.
- Built an internal LLM-powered RAG system (LangChain, FAISS) on Kubernetes; optimized indexing and retrieval latency, enabling 50% faster knowledge discovery and onboarding.
- Partnered directly with C‑level stakeholders to align AI roadmaps with business KPIs, presenting data‑driven ROI reports and leading a team of 20 data scientists and analysts.

### Rubbles (SBDA Group) — Lead ML Engineer
*Apr 2022 – Jan 2023 | Istanbul, Turkey*

- Engineered and deployed production‑grade ML services with Spark and Docker, ensuring high‑throughput data processing and seamless backend integration; reduced inventory shortfalls by 15% for a major confectionery brand.
- Mentored a team of 5+ developers, instituting code review practices, unit testing, and CI/CD pipelines that improved code robustness and deployment velocity.

### Rubbles (SBDA Group) — Senior ML Engineer
*Nov 2021 – Apr 2022 | Moscow, Russia*

- Architected a global‑scale demand forecasting system for a top QSR chain using PySpark; advanced feature engineering improved forecast accuracy (WAPE) by 12%.
- Implemented real‑time traffic features that increased campaign ROI and reduced perishable food waste by 7%, directly linking model performance to business outcomes.

### NDA (Confidential Oil & Gas Client) — Senior ML Engineer
*Jun 2017 – Nov 2021 | Moscow, Russia*

- Led a cross‑functional team of 6+ engineers to develop dynamic ML models for energy consumption, achieving a 5‑7% reduction in energy costs through predictive optimization.
- Architected a Digital Twin MVP for oil refining on Kubernetes and Kafka, delivering a scalable, high‑availability simulation platform that accelerated R&D cycles.
- Designed and deployed an anomaly detection system using TensorFlow/Keras that reduced equipment downtime by 12%, strengthening operational resilience.

## Skills

**Programming Languages:** Python (expert), C++ (proficient), SQL (advanced)  
**ML Frameworks & Tools:** PyTorch, TensorFlow, Transformers (Hugging Face), vLLM, LangChain, FAISS, LightGBM  
**Distributed Systems & MLOps:** Docker, Kubernetes, PySpark, Databricks, Kafka, GitLab CI/CD  
**Domain Expertise:** Large Language Models (LLMs), Transformer & State‑Space Architectures (Mamba), Retrieval‑Augmented Generation (RAG), Distributed Data Processing

## Education

- **PhD Candidate** in Computer Science — SPbPU (ABD), 2021  
- **M.Sc.** in Technical Systems Management (Honours) — SPbPU, Russia, 2017  
- **B.Sc.** in Computer Sciences — SPbPU, Russia, 2015  
- **Erasmus Exchange** — Czech Technical University in Prague, 2013

## Additional Information

- **Languages:** English (C1 – taught and presented internationally); Russian (native).  
- **Relocation:** Fully prepared to self‑fund relocation to Heidelberg and commit to regular on‑site collaboration.  
- **Teaching & Mentoring:** Designed and delivered a 30+ lecture Generative AI & ML course at EPIC Institute of Technology, covering training efficiency and model optimization techniques.
